\]

**Verification.**  
\(|T_k|=k(k+1)/2\) is correct (triangular number).  
Each sunny line can cover at most \(\bigl\lfloor (k+1)/2\bigr\rfloor\) points by (2.5).  
Thus the total number of points that can be covered by the \(k\) sunny lines is at most \(k\bigl\lfloor (k+1)/2\bigr\rfloor\).  
To cover all points we need the opposite inequality, which is exactly (3.2).  

The subsequent case analysis (even \(k\) impossible, odd \(k=2m+1\) forces equality) follows algebraically and is correct.

**Conclusion.** No error in this step.

